# Copy to .env (gitignored). Everything has a working default.
#
# The model configuration is NOT here - it lives in settings/, one file per
# serving workspace, and ./use.sh copies the one you pick to
# dsh-home/settings.yaml. This file is only for the values compose.yml needs.
#
#   ./use.sh                                 what is available, what is active
#   ./use.sh vllm-2node-qwen38-flash-next    the default
#   ./up.sh                                  deploy it, pointed at a model

# WHERE THE HARNESS RUNS. It is a client - no GPU, no unified memory - so it
# belongs on a node that is not holding a rank. Anything but `local` is an ssh
# target (key-based).
# HARNESS_HOST=gb10-homer

# The server it talks to, WITHOUT /v1. Unset means the recipe's loopback URL
# when local, else the head's nordlynx address - the mesh path ufw already
# allows. README, "Reaching the server", has the LAN alternative.
# HARNESS_ENDPOINT=http://<head-mesh-address>:8903

# Which file in settings/ up.sh deploys. Default: the 1017 recipe.
# HARNESS_SETTINGS=tensorfold-2node-dsv41-flash-1017

# The web UI port. 3080 is dsh's default, but it is not reserved: on
# gb10-homer VS Code's extension-host node service holds a wide forwarded-port
# set (3080, 3081, 8896, 8903, ...), so the harness uses 39090. Tunnel to the
# same number.
# DSH_PORT=39090

# What the agent may read and write. THE ONE SETTING WORTH THINKING ABOUT: an
# agent harness with tool access does what it likes inside this directory.
# The default ./work starts empty on purpose. Give it a project, not $HOME.
# DSH_WORKSPACE=/home/you/src/some-project

# Any non-empty string. A locally served model ignores the value; the client
# library refuses to send a request without one.
# LOCAL_API_KEY=gx10

# Only if you also configure the hosted provider in settings.yaml. Leaving this
# unset is a reasonable way to guarantee nothing reaches DeepSeek.
# DEEPSEEK_API_KEY=sk-...

# Pin the harness once a version works for you. Unset means `latest`, which for
# a developer preview means "whatever shipped this week" - and 0.2.1 moved
# provider config out of settings.yaml into Cordis patch layers, rejecting the
# llm-pi-ai section this workspace's settings/ catalogue uses. 0.1.5-rc.1 is
# the version it is written for.
# DSH_VERSION=0.1.5-rc.1   # the published tags are all -rc/-alpha; `0.1.0` is not one

# Who the container runs as. Defaults to 1000:1000, which is the usual first
# user on these boxes. Set it if `id -u` says otherwise, or ./dsh-home fills
# with files you cannot edit.
# DSH_UID=1000
# DSH_GID=1000

# NODE_IMAGE=node:22-slim
# START_PERIOD=12m
